Package: SwitchEconometrics
Type: Package
Title: Unified Estimation of Endogenous Regime-Dependent Economic Systems
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ibrahim", "Niankara", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "Ibrahim.niankara@aau.ac.ae"),
    person("BRASS Digital Lab", role = "fnd",
           comment = "LLC registered in Burkina Faso, RCCM BF-OUA-01-2026-B13-02466; https://brassbe1982-bdlweb.share.connect.posit.cloud/"))
Description: A unified framework for endogenous switching regression,
    endogenous treatment, sample selection, multinomial switching,
    copula-based dependence and longitudinal switching, built on one general
    statistical model of regime selection and regime-specific outcomes.
    The development versions build the classical binary endogenous switching
    regression model (Lokshin and Sajaia (2004)
    <doi:10.1177/1536867X0400400306>; Heckman (1979) <doi:10.2307/1912352>)
    layer by layer: model specification, distribution and
    parameter-transformation engines, the likelihood with analytic score and
    Hessian (this version), then full-information maximum-likelihood and
    two-step estimators, inference, treatment effects and counterfactuals.
